+# Trust anchor for the T-7 label-approval gate (.claude/scripts/approval_gate.py).
+#
+# UNARMED while this file holds no key line. In that state approval_gate.py
+# reports UNVERIFIABLE, the close path prints a notice, and nothing is refused —
+# installing the gate changed no existing behaviour.
+#
+# ARM IT by appending ONE line, in ssh allowed_signers format:
+#
+#     hank@cxforge ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nz...
+#
+# The key MUST be passphrase-protected and MUST NOT be loaded into ssh-agent.
+# A key the agent's ssh-agent holds is a key the agent can sign with — measured,
+# not assumed: an unconfirmed agent key produced a "Good signature" and a
+# `%G? = G` git commit in this environment with no prompt and no touch.
+#
+# See README.md in this directory for the two commands.
+#
+# This file and everything beside it are harness_lib.HUMAN_ONLY: Edit/Write is
+# denied under every claim, and any ticket window that changes them fails the
+# close-time integrity check. That does not make substitution impossible (Bash
+# is not covered by any PreToolUse matcher) — it makes it close-blocking and
+# visible in the diff.
